  <sharedRules>
<rule id="ac0f-ecf4-4a58-e7bd" name="Dominus-class" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>Heavier than a Questoris but lighter than an Acastus. Ion Bulwark: the Knight has an Ion Shield as a Questoris Knight, but the save applies against attacks from every direction rather than one arc. Reactor Overload: when the Knight is destroyed, roll a D6; on a 4+, every unit within 2D6&quot; suffers D6 hits at Strength 9, AP 2, as an Acastus Knight&apos;s reactor blast. Siege Engine: the Knight may fire every weapon it carries in each Shooting phase, but may not Advance.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="9f8a-2498-0943-05ed" name="Questoris-class" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>Questoris-class Knights use the official Questoris Ion Shield value and follow every rule that applies to Questoris Knights.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="50e6-3d36-7112-70ae" name="War Dog-class" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>War Dogs are the Traitor equivalent of the Armiger Helverin and Warglaive, fielded as an Armiger Talon of 1 to 4 models in the same slot as Armigers, using the official Armiger Talon, Fleet (2) and ionic deflector rules. Pack Hunters: a War Dog unit may re-roll to-hit rolls of 1 against an enemy unit that has already been shot at by another War Dog unit this phase.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d85c-46a6-7d65-5cf9" name="Bound to Ruin" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>A Chaos Knight is always Traitor and may only be fielded in a Traitor Household or a Traitor army.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="1526-384c-3eb9-2f77" name="Questor Traitoris (Household Trait)" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>A Traitor Household that includes at least one Chaos Knight may take this trait instead of an official Household trait. Dread Household: every Knight in the Household has Fear or an equivalent rule forcing engaged enemies to take a Leadership test before fighting. Fallen Nobility: the Household may include War Dogs in place of Armigers, and may not include any Imperial Knight from this conversion. Infernal Pacts: each Chaos Knight in the Household may take one Pact of Ruin at half cost.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="df9d-f3a6-b896-ecbd" name="Chainbreaker" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>Canis Rex may re-roll failed to-hit and to-wound rolls against enemy Knights, Titans and characters.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="f493-26dc-8ec6-43ea" name="Freeblade" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>Canis Rex may join any Loyalist army or Household, but never gains a Household trait.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="e08a-87ac-bf8e-d99b" name="The Last Hunt" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>Canis Rex has It Will Not Die (6+), restoring Hull Points.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="8978-5000-f525-34c3" name="Saturation Fire" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>The Destrier&apos;s ranged weapons gain Ignores Cover against units within 3&quot; of an objective marker.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="3a8c-9331-b94f-5d83" name="Thundercharge" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>If the Destrier carries both a Bellatus reaper chainsword and a thundershock spear, it gains Rage (2).</description>
</rule>
<rule id="91cb-37ce-7b0d-f743" name="Aura of Madness" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>Enemy psykers within 18&quot; suffer Perils of the Warp on any double when making a Psychic check.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="afc0-7215-ece4-11aa" name="Warp Conduit" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>The Abominant knows the Warp Storm psychic weapon, and uses a Leadership of 9 for Psychic checks.</description>
</rule>
<rule id="d80e-0f1f-f849-6d5b" name="Rampage" publicationId="9d5c-8cad-e48b-25fc" hidden="false">
<description>The Rampager adds 1 to its charge distance rolls, and gains Hammer of Wrath (D3) in addition to any it has.</description>
</rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
